    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Over the last few decades, city planning and management have increasingly focused on\r\nresilience and sustainability, as it has become more apparent that climate change has - and will continue to have - significant impacts on cities. Mountain View has a robust legacy of creating and implementing initiatives that enhance the community's ability to adapt to climate changes. The city has made remarkable progress in becoming more resilient and has outlined future policies and projects to build on this progress, as detailed in the “Strategic Pathways Through 2030” report and the “Environmental Sustainability Action Plan”, which is updated and revised every three years. Although Mountain View is ahead of the curve in recognizing and taking action toward becoming more resilient, there remains more to be done. This report aims to create a mechanism that enables Mountain View to evaluate and prioritize policies and initiatives based on their potential impact, as well as assess the policies and initiatives that have already been implemented.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Yin Moh, J., Jensen, S., Olomu, M., and Limric, B. (2024). Resiliency Roadmap: Analysis of the Status Quo and Recommendations Moving Forward. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/qt235tv1296. https://doi.org/10.25740/qt235tv1296.",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
